WEBVTT

1
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:52,720
[BLADE OF FURY]

2
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,570
As a bounty hunter,

3
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:56,220
I risk my life for money.

4
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,680
The world is in chaos now.

5
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:03,990
There are outlaws everywhere.

6
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:15,150
The government pays me

7
00:02:15,310 --> 00:02:17,010
to catch the outlaws.

8
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:21,140
Those who do this kind of jobs are called bounty hunters.

9
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,610
You don't get it?

10
00:02:30,610 --> 00:02:32,060
We're like businessmen.

11
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:35,020
And the business we do is highly risky.

12
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:36,840
I came to you

13
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,060
to discuss a deal with you.

14
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,290
There is a batch of goods.

15
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:42,610
It belongs to the government.

16
00:02:42,610 --> 00:02:44,080
It's a batch of jewels.

17
00:02:44,150 --> 00:02:47,350
Those who transported the goods were robbed on their way.

18
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:50,030
After you robbed them and killed them,

19
00:02:50,030 --> 00:02:53,030
you also killed the Persian merchants.

20
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:56,110
Then you pretended to be foreign merchants

21
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:58,700
and tried to escape to the Western Region.

22
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:00,770
This is such a risky move.

23
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:09,660
Leave the jewels here.

24
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:11,620
And I'll pretend we've never met.

25
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:15,070
This is what I want to talk to you about.

26
00:03:18,370 --> 00:03:20,280
Are you really a bounty hunter?

27
00:03:30,070 --> 00:03:33,010
Many bounty hunters were killed by this knife.

28
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:34,630
I'm not afraid of anyone.

29
00:03:34,850 --> 00:03:36,860
Except those four.

30
00:03:37,230 --> 00:03:38,530
Who are those four?

31
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:40,330
The fearless Jackal.

32
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:41,810
The cunning Ghost Lady.

33
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:43,610
The cruel Blind.

34
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,920
And the brutal Grey-Haired Master.

35
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:49,710
It's obvious that you're not a woman.

36
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:51,610
You're neither gray-haired

37
00:03:51,610 --> 00:03:52,900
nor blind.

38
00:03:53,150 --> 00:03:55,250
Are you Jackal?

39
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:13,190
I don't think we cannot reach a deal today.

40
00:05:20,530 --> 00:05:22,790
You're crazy!

41
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,170
I am...

42
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:57,110
Jackal!

43
00:05:57,430 --> 00:05:58,440
[Jackal]

44
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,690
You're smart.
[Jackal]

45
00:05:59,690 --> 00:06:00,080
[Jackal]

46
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:07,490
I was ignorant.

47
00:06:07,770 --> 00:06:09,930
I'll give you all these goods.

48
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,930
Please let me go.

49
00:06:12,690 --> 00:06:14,070
It's too late.

50
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,520
Jackal.

51
00:06:32,110 --> 00:06:35,940
What the government was transporting is not jewels.

52
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:38,720
It's a woman being transported.

53
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:43,230
Let's talk.

54
00:06:44,110 --> 00:06:46,020
Let me go.

55
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,050
That woman

56
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:50,650
knows a secret.

57
00:06:50,650 --> 00:06:54,120
The secret is more valuable than jewels.

58
00:06:54,530 --> 00:06:55,930
What's more,

59
00:06:55,930 --> 00:06:59,860
she can be really sexy and wild.

60
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:02,400
What are you doing?

61
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:04,060
Don't kill him!

62
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:08,110
Oh no.

63
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:09,690
The wanted poster said he must be captured alive.

64
00:07:09,690 --> 00:07:12,150
If he's dead, I won't get any bounties at all.

65
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:16,730
Stop.

66
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,980
You have to compensate me.

67
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,060
Let go of me!

68
00:07:39,610 --> 00:07:41,150
You can't drink wine.

69
00:07:51,650 --> 00:07:52,570
You don't have money.

70
00:07:52,570 --> 00:07:53,760
You can't go there.

71
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,550
He's ahead of us again.

72
00:08:13,190 --> 00:08:15,390
This is Chu Xiong, the notorious thief?

73
00:08:16,270 --> 00:08:17,290
Yes.

74
00:08:24,030 --> 00:08:26,030
How could you tell such a stupid lie?

75
00:08:27,190 --> 00:08:28,830
She killed Chu Xiong.

76
00:08:29,190 --> 00:08:30,310
One for one.

77
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:31,690
I brought her to show that I've done my job.

78
00:08:31,690 --> 00:08:33,420
Ask her if you don't believe me.

79
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:37,520
You jerk!

80
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:41,980
It's okay if you only give me half of the agreed bounty.

81
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:43,190
Miss, you're right.

82
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:44,570
He's called Jackal.

83
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,740
Of course he's even worse than a pig or a dog.

84
00:08:46,740 --> 00:08:48,980
It's hard to be a human nowadays.

85
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,230
It's easier to be a pig or a dog.

86
00:08:50,230 --> 00:08:52,030
You jerk!

87
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,260
If you don't pay me,

88
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:54,530
I won't leave.

89
00:08:55,070 --> 00:08:56,260
What are you doing?

90
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:58,140
She can kill people.

91
00:08:58,620 --> 00:09:00,610
She killed a notorious criminal.

92
00:09:00,610 --> 00:09:02,080
According to the law, she'll be treated leniently.

93
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,610
She won't have to go to jail.

94
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,470
Though bad people are everywhere nowadays,

95
00:09:05,470 --> 00:09:07,330
